<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>About SolveLink — Real Problems. Local Minds. Real Impact.</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Learn about SolveLink, the civic innovation platform connecting citizen challenges with universities, researchers, and government authorities. (SIH26043)">
  
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/global.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/components.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/challenges.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/responsive.css">
</head>
<body>

  <!-- Navigation -->
  <%- include('partials/navbar', { activePath: '/about' }) %>

  <!-- Header Section -->
  <header class="challenges-header">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <span class="badge badge-primary" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-2);">Problem Statement &bull; SIH26043</span>
      <h1 class="challenges-header-title">Bridging Local Problems with Local Minds</h1>
      <p class="challenges-header-desc">
        SolveLink is a collaborative civic-technology infrastructure designed to bridge societal challenges, government authorities, academic institutions, and industry innovators.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- Main Content -->
  <main id="main-content" class="main-content section">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      
      <!-- Section 1: The Core Bridge -->
      <section style="margin-bottom: var(--space-12);">
        <h2 style="font-size: var(--font-size-2xl); font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">The 5-Stage Civic Bridge</h2>
        <div class="editorial-prose">
          <p>
            Traditional public systems frequently fail because the people closest to a community problem (citizens) have no direct pipeline to the people with the technical capabilities to solve it (university researchers, engineering students, and local innovators). Meanwhile, government authorities are burdened with repetitive issues without the capacity to commission bespoke engineering research for every local bottleneck.
          </p>
          <p>
            SolveLink creates a structured, verified lifecycle connecting all stakeholders:
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Visual Progression Grid -->
        <div class="workflow-steps" style="margin: var(--space-6) 0;">
          <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="workflow-num">1</span>
            <h3 class="workflow-name">Society</h3>
            <p class="workflow-desc">Citizens observe and report ground-level infrastructure and societal challenges.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="workflow-num">2</span>
            <h3 class="workflow-name">Government</h3>
            <p class="workflow-desc">Authorities verify the issue and publish it as an official Innovation Challenge.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="workflow-num">3</span>
            <h3 class="workflow-name">Academia</h3>
            <p class="workflow-desc">University labs, students, and industry partners formulate technical proposals.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="workflow-num">4</span>
            <h3 class="workflow-name">Solution</h3>
            <p class="workflow-desc">Proposals are evaluated rigorously on feasibility, cost, and community impact.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="workflow-num">5</span>
            <h3 class="workflow-name">Impact</h3>
            <p class="workflow-desc">Approved solutions receive pilot deployment grants and milestone tracking.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Why SolveLink is NOT a Grievance Portal -->
      <section style="margin-bottom: var(--space-12);">
        <h2 style="font-size: var(--font-size-2xl); font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">How SolveLink Differs from a Normal Grievance Portal</h2>
        <div class="editorial-prose">
          <p>
            Most civic portals operate as passive complaint depositories—tickets are logged, assigned to an already overworked department officer, and closed with bureaucratic responses without tackling root causes.
          </p>
          <p>
            SolveLink is not a complaints box; it is an <strong>Innovation Procurement Engine</strong>:
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="comparison-table-wrapper">
          <table class="comparison-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th style="width: 25%;">Dimension</th>
                <th style="width: 37.5%;">Standard Grievance Portal</th>
                <th style="width: 37.5%;">SolveLink Platform</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Primary Objective</strong></td>
                <td><span class="comparison-badge-bad">Ticket Disposal</span><br>Closing complaints to meet departmental SLA quotas.</td>
                <td><span class="comparison-badge-good">Root-Cause Innovation</span><br>Engineering scalable, sustainable solutions.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Ecosystem Involvement</strong></td>
                <td><span class="comparison-badge-bad">Isolated Silos</span><br>Only government officers handle the complaint.</td>
                <td><span class="comparison-badge-good">Multi-Stakeholder</span><br>Engages universities, student labs, and local industry.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Problem Transformation</strong></td>
                <td><span class="comparison-badge-bad">Static Complaint</span><br>Sits in queue without technical decomposition.</td>
                <td><span class="comparison-badge-good">Innovation Challenge</span><br>AI analyzes category and authorities set technical scope.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Implementation Mechanism</strong></td>
                <td><span class="comparison-badge-bad">Routine Maintenance</span><br>Temporary quick-fixes that break again.</td>
                <td><span class="comparison-badge-good">Funded Pilot Projects</span><br>Structured milestone tracking with measurable KPIs.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Citizen Visibility</strong></td>
                <td><span class="comparison-badge-bad">Opaque Status</span><br>Vague "In Progress" or "Resolved" flags.</td>
                <td><span class="comparison-badge-good">Open Accountability</span><br>Public progress tracking, solution reviews, and community upvotes.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Pillars of SolveLink -->
      <section>
        <h2 style="font-size: var(--font-size-2xl); font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">Guiding Principles</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="card card-body">
            <h3 style="font-size: var(--font-size-md); font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-primary);">Trust & Verification</h3>
            <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: var(--font-size-sm); margin-bottom: 0;">
              Every challenge is validated by designated government authorities before being published to prevent spam and ensure administrative alignment.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card card-body">
            <h3 style="font-size: var(--font-size-md); font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-primary);">Academic Synergy</h3>
            <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: var(--font-size-sm); margin-bottom: 0;">
              Academic research is applied directly to solve regional municipal problems, rewarding university teams with grants, recognition, and patents.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <%- include('partials/footer') %>

  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
